# Link-checker ignore list — every entry verified alive (or documented) on 2026-08-19; see issue #6.
# Bot-armored domains: block curl/lychee TLS fingerprints but serve real content to browsers
# (each content-verified via secondary fetch 2026-08-19).
https://business.adobe.com/.*
https://quickbooks.intuit.com/.*
https://www.servicenow.com/.*
https://www.turkishairlines.com/.*
https://www.uber.com/.*
# Radware Bot Manager (returns nonstandard 247 to non-browsers); site alive.
https://www.alice.co.il/.*
# unsplash.com — lychee got 401 from the GitHub runner on 2026-09-15 (issue #17); a direct fetch the same day
# returned 200 with real content. Bot-armored against the checker's TLS fingerprint, not dead.
https://unsplash.com/.*
# getyourguide.com — lychee failed with "HTTP/2 protocol error" from the runner on 2026-09-15 (issue #17).
# A direct fetch the same day returned 403, which this workflow already accepts; the break is the HTTP/2
# negotiation, not the status. Site alive.
https://www.getyourguide.com/.*
# www.adobe.com — resets curl/lychee on both HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 (INTERNAL_ERROR) from a residential network on
# 2026-09-25; a second fetch channel (Exa crawl) the same day returned the real homepage. Same class as business.adobe.com.
https://www.adobe.com/.*
# elixion.ai — reset the connection (os error 104) from the GitHub runner on 2026-09-25 (issue #20) after passing there
# on 2026-09-21, and resets curl/lychee from a residential network too; an Exa crawl the same day returned the real
# homepage ("The project tracker Claude runs for you"). Intermittent bot armor, not dead.
https://elixion.ai/.*
# valossa.com — 401 Unauthorized to lychee from the GitHub runner on 2026-09-07 (#13) and 2026-09-25 (#22); an Exa crawl
# on 2026-09-25 returned the real page ("Video AI Assistant ... | Valossa"). Auth-walls bots, not dead.
https://valossa.com/.*
# fred.stlouisfed.org — "HTTP/2 protocol error" to lychee from the GitHub runner on 2026-09-28 (#24) and 2026-10-05 (#29),
# and curl gets no response from a residential network; an Exa crawl on 2026-10-08 returned the live FRED homepage.
# Same class as getyourguide.com: the break is the HTTP/2 negotiation, not the site.
https://fred.stlouisfed.org/.*
# saturation.io — "HTTP/2 protocol error" to lychee from the GitHub runner on 2026-10-19 (#36); a direct fetch the same
# day returned 200 with the live site. Same class as getyourguide.com and FRED: the break is the HTTP/2 negotiation.
https://saturation.io/.*
# www.vinilogy.com — "HTTP/2 protocol error" to lychee from the GitHub runner on 2026-10-12 (#32) and 2026-10-19 (#36);
# a direct fetch on 2026-10-19 returned 200. Same HTTP/2-negotiation class, site alive.
https://www.vinilogy.com/.*
# qikcms.com — "Request timed out" to lychee from the GitHub runner on 2026-11-02 (#43), 11-09 (#48) and 11-16 (#52);
# a direct fetch on 2026-11-22 returned 200 with the product's own title. Slow or filtered toward the runner, not dead.
https://qikcms.com/.*
# www.finhay.com.vn — 503 to lychee from the GitHub runner in the same three reports; a direct fetch on 2026-11-22
# returned 200 with the Finhay homepage. Refuses the runner's network, not dead.
https://www.finhay.com.vn/.*
# www.magicpatterns.com — "HTTP/2 protocol error" from the runner on 2026-11-09 (#48) and 11-16 (#52); a direct fetch on
